      "mergedPostDetails": "Hello,\n\nI’m currently participating in the VRChat open beta and noticed a bug affecting all items (including PETs):\n\nWhen you spawn an item, everything works as expected.\n\nHowever, when you remove it locally, it disappears for yourself, but it remains visible to other players.\n\nAs a result, it’s possible to spawn an infinite number of items globally, since others still see the old ones.\n\nIt seems that this issue doesn’t affect everyone — for some players, it works correctly or the bug happens only temporarily.\n\nThis problem appears to occur only in the open beta, and not in the stable version as far as I can tell.\n\nI wanted to report this in case it helps identify and fix the issue.\n\nThanks to the team for all your hard work, and good luck with the debugging!\n\nLink to video : \n\n- https://youtu.be/VpP8Fa7XbPs\n\n- https://youtu.be/wA4KrC_4qSU",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Bug in the Open Beta – Items do not despawn globally",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "69128bb5ab8b0798b8f0eec6",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Additional note:\n\nWhen this happened, my friend saw many of my PETs duplicated.\n\nAfter I disconnected, all of my PETs moved toward him and started following him as if they were his own.\n\nThis might be related to the same sync issue, but it’s a strange behavior worth mentioning.\n\nLink to show the issue lol : https://youtu.be/cl63JzhWBMM",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
